{
  "_comment": "Boons of Salvation: 31 recorded boons across four groups. Six of them are discounts on the blessings of named gods, which is the only place in the record where those gods appear by name.",
  "_mechanics": {
    "what": "Boons of Salvation are permanent, account-wide upgrades bought with Karma Shards at the Shrine of Causality.",
    "scope": "They apply across all four Part I routes, which is what makes them a long-term investment rather than a route upgrade.",
    "toggling": "A boon can be switched on and off once unlocked. Toggling is not the same as buying again.",
    "unlocks": "The tier requirements below are the source~s own estimates rather than confirmed figures, and it says so on the page it publishes them on.",
    "shardUse": "Karma Shards have two uses: buying boons, and Merge Causality from Part III onwards. Once every boon is unlocked, extra shards have nowhere to go but a merge.",
    "refunds": "Whether shards spent on a merge come back on a restart is not recorded anywhere, so the safe reading is that they do not."
  },
  "_openGaps": [
    "Fifteen of the thirty-one boons have no published price at all.",
    "No second or third tier has a published price anywhere, so a full unlock total cannot be calculated. The sixteen known first tiers add up to about 5,000 Karma Shards.",
    "Whether a boon can be bought more than once is not recorded.",
    "Whether shards are refunded on a restart is not recorded."
  ],
